  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">STRENGHTEN THE PROTECTION MEASURES IN MANAS NATIONAL PARK AS A PART OF THE PROGRAM INDIAN RHINO VISION&apos;</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO CONTINUE TO SUPPORT THE SALARY OF 15 ADDITIONAL GUARDS (WHO ARE IN ADDITION TO THE EXISTING STAFF OF THE FOREST DEPARTMENT) FOR 24 MONTHS, TO PATROL AND MONITOR THE RHINO HABITATS IN MANAS NATIONAL PARK (MNP). PREFERENCE WILL BE GIVEN TO PERSONS FROM THE ADJACENT VILLAGES TO IMPROVE THE SOCIOECONOMIC STATUS OF THE VILLAGERS, AND TO DEVELOP A GOOD RELATIONSHIP BETWEEN THE MNP MANAGEMENT AND THE VILLAGERS ADJACENT TO MNP. SPECIAL TRAINING OF THE NEWLY RECRUITED GUARDS ON WILDLIFE CONSERVATION AND TO COMBAT POACHING WILL BE PROVIDED BY THE FOREST DEPARTMENT.</narrative>
  </description>
